      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A uniform Gaussian heuristic for log|zeta| recovers the conjectural quadratic logarithmic moment exponent through exponential moments, but not the arithmetic-normalized constant. Beyond that bulk calculation, the finite-N unitary model has a fixed-N small-value regime controlled by the nearest generating-function pole, while zeta large-value estimates exhibit different quadratic and V log V decay regimes.",
