    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b2e8dbf4fd3e9a7c9ed314fc765cd1d7f4b813cfb49dae8d5d655af3aec83b95",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "After matching unitary matrix size to the local mean zero density, characteristic-polynomial moments predict the combinatorial factor left after zeta's prime-dependent factor is separated. A distinct constrained-Dirichlet-series calculation makes an analogous split algebraically: its regular Euler product tends to the arithmetic constant, while pairwise zeta poles supply the leading singular contour.",
