      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c22a698ca23902b9d5b5c35b0b72750ca1f70c7b81dc41e5edc3dea2a295105e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Density-scaled displacement from a zero has a zero-offset endpoint governed by derivative moments, while unitary characteristic-polynomial calculations provide explicit conjectural constants for those moments. Wirtinger-type arguments then use global integrals of the Hardy Z-function and its derivative, together with such moment constants, to force lower bounds for exceptional normalized gaps.",
