      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cc4f11fc3b3c366055b479d020433977d7adb48c20fd0975cd358fc16d9a617c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Layer-cake integration reconstructs a positive shifted moment from measures of weighted log-zeta level sets, whereas Markov's inequality sends high even moments of prime polynomials in the opposite direction to upper bounds for exceptional sets. In both uses, the effective variance and the allowable polynomial or interval length determine which moment order and prime-block truncation are admissible.",
